# Next.js App Router Patterns

## App Router Structure
- **Pages**: Use `page.tsx` for route components
- **Layouts**: Use `layout.tsx` for shared layouts
- **Loading**: Use `loading.tsx` for loading states
- **Error**: Use `error.tsx` for error boundaries
- **Not Found**: Use `not-found.tsx` for 404 pages

## Route Organization
- **Public Routes**: `/login`, `/unauthorized`
- **Protected Routes**: `/dashboard/*` (requires authentication)
- **Dynamic Routes**: Use `[id]` for dynamic segments
- **Nested Routes**: Use folder structure for nested layouts

## Layout Patterns
- **Root Layout**: [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx) - Global providers and structure
- **Dashboard Layout**: [src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/dashboard/layout.tsx) - Protected route wrapper
- **Conditional Layout**: [src/components/layout/ConditionalLayout.tsx](mdc:src/components/layout/ConditionalLayout.tsx) - Auth-based layout

## Client vs Server Components
- **Client Components**: Use `'use client'` directive
- **Server Components**: Default for pages and layouts
- **Hybrid Approach**: Use server components for data fetching, client for interactivity

## Data Fetching
- Use server components for initial data loading
- Use client components for user interactions
- Implement proper loading states
- Handle errors gracefully

## Metadata and SEO
- Use `metadata` export for page metadata
- Set proper titles and descriptions
- Use Open Graph tags for social sharing
- Implement proper canonical URLs

## Performance Optimization
- Use Next.js Image component for images
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use dynamic imports for code splitting
- Optimize bundle size

## Authentication Integration
- Use middleware for route protection
- Implement proper redirects
- Handle authentication state
- Use protected route patterns

## Error Handling
- Use error boundaries for component errors
- Implement proper error pages
- Handle authentication errors
- Provide user-friendly error messages

## Styling in App Router
- Use global CSS in [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css)
- Use Tailwind CSS for component styling
- Implement proper CSS loading
- Use CSS modules when needed

## API Routes (Future)
- Use `route.ts` for API endpoints
- Implement proper request/response handling
- Use proper HTTP methods
- Handle errors and validation